		(property "Description" "Addressable RGB LED (NeoPixel-compatible), Yellow key. Replaces the discrete LED+2SC1815+resistor driver (2026-10-01, user decision: WS2812B 5050 SMD chosen over SK6812MINI-E -- the latter is already used in complicated_wires but judged too hard to hand-solder; commonising on WS2812B going forward). Daisy-chained GP6->R10->D1->D2->D3->D4 (chain order = dict order Red/Blue/Green/Yellow); firmware addresses each LED by chain position, colour is software-assigned (not fixed by the LED itself). Pin1=VDD(+5V), pin2=DOUT, pin3=VSS(GND), pin4=DIN. Placed near the Yellow(right) key (not aligned to the switch's LED window -- user decision: thin keycap + indirect lighting, see four_button_design_notes.md)."
			(at 0 0 0)
			(unlocked yes)
			(layer "F.Fab")
			(hide yes)
			(uuid "baa6c33a-7896-456a-87f8-bc40c02b14e1")
			(effects
				(font
					(size 1.27 1.27)
					(thickness 0.15)
				)
			)
		)
